    {
      "scene": 1,
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 1.4615,
      "text": "Why isn't this a Spring bean?"
    },
    {
      "scene": 2,
      "start": 1.5415,
      "end": 7.17225,
      "text": "The class compiles, but the context has no registration for it. Asking for Client fails."
    },
    {
      "scene": 3,
      "start": 7.25225,
      "end": 13.295667,
      "text": "Register Factory Config, then refresh. Its bean method returns the Client that Spring manages."
    },
    {
      "scene": 4,
      "start": 13.375667,
      "end": 20.587292,
      "text": "Or add the component annotation to Worker, then configure a scan of its package. Spring discovers and registers it."
    },
    {
      "scene": 5,
      "start": 20.667292,
      "end": 26.983,
      "text": "The scan covers lesson dot scan. Outside lives in another package, so its annotation isn't picked up."
    },
    {
      "scene": 6,
      "start": 27.063,
      "end": 35.89,
      "text": "Our three tests pass: both registered beans are found; the class outside the scan stays missing. Registration tells Spring what to manage."
    },
    {
      "scene": 7,
      "start": 37.89,
      "end": 38.98075,
      "text": "Thanks for watching."
    }
  ],
